                                        "entry_id": "1ad626b7-ea0e-3d11-bc67-d2cb16f354f9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A game to encourage small children to eat, in which the parent or carer pretends a spoonful of food is an aircraft flying into the child's mouth."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Canada",
                                            "Philippines",
                                            "US"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ffce3c59-85ee-4c0c-b3ae-c0e848735e9a",
                                                "sense_id": "8db5b136-3531-3206-b392-13cd9a6b35d1",
                                                "text": "So, he'd take a spoon and he'd start playing airplane, circling the spoon around in the air until it was ready to land in the runway of my mouth."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e666fc92-b527-4ca0-9def-41647d9afaee",
                                                "sense_id": "8db5b136-3531-3206-b392-13cd9a6b35d1",
                                                "text": "Willis wondered what this fellow wanted to do, spoon feed him? Play airplane?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9ca9f881-c344-42c5-98ab-cc5629fda0e7",
                                                "sense_id": "8db5b136-3531-3206-b392-13cd9a6b35d1",
                                                "text": "For instance, Jan has taken to playing airplane with the spoon to get Charley to attend to the spoon and want to take it into his mouth."
                                            }
